<title>MEXICO: Emvasa sees new $10 mln plant in 1998.</title>
<headline>Emvasa sees new $10 mln plant in 1998.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican soft drinks bottler Embotelladores del Valle de Anahuac S.A. de C.V. plans to invest $10 million in a new plant in 1998, a company director said on Monday.</p>
<p>The director, who asked not to be named, said the plant could be located at Leon, in the state of Guanajuato, some 200 miles northwest of Mexico City.</p>
<p>((--Tomas de la Rosa, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7912))</p>
